.TH MGS.STATE 4 2026-10-09 Lustre "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
mgs.state \- show whether the MGS is operating as leader or follower
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY "lctl get_param mgs.MGS.state"
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.BR 0444 " | " -r--r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
Per MGS service
.TP
.B Config
Present wherever an MGS runs: on the MGS node, and on any MDT or OST
node that runs an MGS follower
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mgs.MGS.state
parameter shows whether the MGS service is operating as the
.B leader
or as a
.BR follower .
.PP
One MGS is the
.B leader
that handles configuration updates.
On each other server node, one MDT or OST mounted with
.B mgs_follower
runs an MGS
.BR follower ,
unless also mounted with
.BR nomgs ,
.B nosvc
or read-only (see
.BR mount.lustre (8)).
A follower is a readonly backup that serves the client, params and sptlrpc
logs to clients.
.PP
The
.B mgs.state
parameter is read-only and is set internally by the MGS subsystem
based on whether the node is MGS leader.
.SH MODULES
This parameter is in the following modules:
.EX
.B mgs.MGS.state
.EE
.SH EXAMPLES
Show the state of the MGS that handles configuration updates:
.EX
.RB "mgs# " "lctl get_param mgs.MGS.state"
mgs.MGS.state=leader
.EE
.PP
Show the state of a read-only MGS running on an MDT or OST:
.EX
.RB "oss# " "lctl get_param mgs.MGS.state"
mgs.MGS.state=follower
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B mgs.state
is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.18.0.
.\" Added in commit 2.17.59
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lctl-get_param (8),
.BR lctl-set_param (8),
.BR mount.lustre (8)
